# Absolute-position frames from the clone, 2026-11-18
#
# Firmware v0.9.7 (bring-up firmware, src/main.cpp), command
# `pos <mask> <0-255>`: ID 50 MASK POS for 1490 ms, then ID 32 MASK POS for
# 300 ms, rotating ch 33/52/71. Frame layout from spitcool/hd-platinum-rf
# (docs/rf-protocol.md, "Position packets correlated with original-bridge
# commands - 2026-10-23"), decoded there from the Platinum bridge.
#
# Clone ID: the working remote's (redacted as yy yy), which is paired to the
# household's groups by handheld group assignment. No bridge involved.
# Watched: the two group-4 shades (bottom-up, one moving rail; corrected 2026-11-25, John). "# ..." lines are the
# tester's (John's) notes. Timestamps are the PC's; each one marks when the
# command was typed, so the gaps between commands are think time.

